711e71ba74e3539daffd","event_uuid":"ad09d7cc-bda4-4fe6-b650-75f008f13ada","position":{"commit_sha":"8b3ce75cf9d3321bf0dcc442f55cb10873c79696","position":"1787165121635247520-ad09d7cc-bda4-4fe6-b650-75f008f13ada"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f346b7cf1d9828feb7f46124c96968f92e00f9856cf1b81cbbcb8ce62b45e2dc","event_uuid":"16bcd965-011b-440d-a6db-a0573a57ec42","position":{"commit_sha":"ef28b8ed308d530aac57781c2f3a2ec90689328d","position":"1787176135264397001-16bcd965-011b-440d-a6db-a0573a57ec42"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"be9601e5201654adddb1a85b033e027a884e01e2bd9ccf0df26b9dcfb17bbc61","event_uuid":"7ef45bee-dc2b-4a8c-9b9b-9ba437f4081e","position":{"commit_sha":"f08e2e8fa8bfa3413820ea371372ac53a05f20ad","position":"1787184825583747001-7ef45bee-dc2b-4a8c-9b9b-9ba437f4081e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d05bbee00cef7630691e000a7120c63f0befdf0d07f79bcd607ea45517386811","event_uuid":"e45eb5fa-af32-47e3-86dd-8f5e3a11dbbd","position":{"commit_sha":"efb43b22b2bb360545611e2445aed819ea54f0f6","position":"1787184830050217001-e45eb5fa-af32-47e3-86dd-8f5e3a11dbbd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 RCA / design classification\n\nProven mechanism: `Makefile:203` runs `zizmor $(RELEASE_WORKFLOW)` with no explicit operating mode and no GitHub token. Zizmor 1.29 follows its documented selection rule: with GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN/ZIZMOR_GITHUB_TOKEN all absent it creates no GitHub client, defaults offline, warns, and skips exactly five token-backed audits: `impostor-commit`, `ref-confusion`, `known-vulnerable-actions`, `stale-action-refs`, and `ref-version-mismatch`. The remaining 35 audits run, the one intentional excessive-permissions suppression remains, and the process exits 0. Upstream source confirms each skipped audit’s `Audit::new` refuses a missing GitHub client; upstream Usage §Operating Modes defines this tokenless default.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof: (A) bare tokenless zizmor scheduled 35, logged those five skips + the reported warning, and exited 0; (B) explicit `--offline` scheduled the same 35 and exited 0 without the warning; (C) a valid GH token scheduled all 40, made GitHub API requests, produced no warning, and exited 0. A deliberately invalid token scheduled all 40 but then failed the audit on a 401, proving online mode adds network/credential availability to the gate rather than only silencing output. A mismatched action version-comment mutation passed explicit offline but online reported seven `ref-version-mismatch` findings; offline mutations still caught the approved SHA-pin and excessive-permissions invariants.\n\nGerrit/CI proof: `_build-and-test.yml:16-19,40-46,90-91` says the reusable takes no secrets and invokes `make lint` without a token env. Actual successful Gerrit Verified run 32102186979 logged the same offline warning at 2026-08-18T05:17:25Z; successful mirror run 32086994835 did likewise. Thus both local and gating CI currently use identical offline semantics.\n\nLegitimacy classification: `intended-behavior` for the upstream warning/default and `feature-request` / design choice for making the five online audits mandatory. The authoritative story `footed-semiacidic-sable` requires zizmor under local `make lint`, scoped to release.yml, and explicitly names full-SHA pins, persist-credentials:false, and permissions; it never requires a token, network, warning-free output, or the full online audit set. The same warning/five skips occur with its introducing zizmor 1.27, so this is not a later regression. No repository authority resolves whether to expand that approved contract.\n\nRecommended non-fix disposition: keep `make lint` deterministic and explicit with `zizmor --offline` (documenting its existing 35-audit semantics and removing the warning). If the five live-metadata audits are desired, add a separate operation-linked online security target and invoke it from Gerrit/GitHub CI with least-privilege `GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}`; decide explicitly whether API outage/rate-limit is gate-fatal. Do not conditionally token the same `make lint`, because that would silently violate the pin’s stated local↔CI parity. No code change is authorized until the owner chooses the target contract.\n\nObserved residual: changing persist-credentials:false to true did not produce a default-persona zizmor finding in this workflow, although `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py::test_checkouts_disable_persist_credentials` independently enforces the invariant in the full CI suite. Accepted outside this online-mode decision because the invariant remains gated; the misleading “zizmor enforces” comment should be corrected with whichever policy change is approved.","timestamp":1787031774029471001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-19): Wire Gerrit CI to run the 5 token-backed zizmor audits (impostor-commit, ref-confusion, known-vulnerable-actions, stale-action-refs, ref-version-mismatch) by providing a GitHub token to the zizmor step in the Gerrit Verify workflow. Keep local 'make lint' portable/offline (no token required); the online audits run in CI only. This preserves project.portability: CI-enabled capability with an offline local fallback. RESOLUTION: add the token env to the zizmor CI step (Makefile:203 invocation accepts an optional token via env), document the online/offline split, and verify the 5 audits execute in the Gerrit Verify run.","timestamp":1787159047189296001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit as change 1910 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1910), commit bc7377a75c. Operator decision implemented: Makefile picks zizmor offline (portable local, --offline suppresses the misleading warning) vs online (when a GitHub token is in the env), and _build-and-test.yml supplies the read-only job token so CI runs the five token-backed audits. docs/releasing.md documents the split. make lint green (no warning). Awaiting Gerrit gates; will not close until Verified +1.","timestamp":1787161518775049001}],"created_at":1786922832417096001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7011cb8c-8b8d-45a8-be37-7910b864b467","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e06a-1450-5e1b-42fc"},{"link_uuid":"a1e54c88-69f9-4454-a9e3-7336505e88bc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fd2b-acca-e3fc-47c4"}],"description":"## Context\n`make lint` deterministically prints: `WARN audit: zizmor is running in offline mode by default; some audits and auto-fixes will not be available.` The gate still exits successfully, so contributors can report a clean lint run while the tool says part of its audit surface is unavailable. A tracker search for `zizmor offline mode` found no open bug owning the warning. Discovered while verifying `treelike-unamusing-grosbeak`.\n\n## Reproduction\nFrom a provisioned checkout, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and inspect the zizmor step.\n\n## Plan\nUse `rebar-debug` to identify exactly which audits are disabled offline, whether Gerrit CI has network/capabilities to run them, and whether the current invocation is deliberate. If changing online/offline policy affects portability, network access, or CI behavior, return an evidence-backed decision brief rather than silently choosing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Root cause and the exact unavailable audit capabilities are proven against the pinned zizmor version.\n- [x] Local/no-network and Gerrit CI behavior are both evaluated.\n- [x] The warning is eliminated by a reviewed policy or explicitly documented/suppressed only if the warning is proven intentional and coverage-equivalent safeguards are cited.\n- [x] `make lint` and relevant workflow gates remain green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","fd2b-acca-e3fc-47c4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7ef45bee-dc2b-4a8c-9b9b-9ba437f4081e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["warning","ci","security","zizmor"],"ticket_id":"7a03-74f2-e812-4104","ticket_type":"bug","title":"make lint runs zizmor offline and leaves online audits unavailable","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["44364ea6-3ee2-4e67-aade-f3cfee47afcb","b7fa701b-1d4e-4374-917b-6ba682bd522a","e5ba0836-3022-4cb1-9fd1-cbbb6e46b715","cd585269-1ecc-4241-b7a6-83f9201a60b3","d3e8c886-ed27-4899-860d-c39302e550c9","b4f9abb9-2ed5-4047-b956-507547cbec96","ed8f0aca-b5ef-4f57-a2ce-a7e33d4823f7","a1e54c88-69f9-4454-a9e3-7336505e88bc","ad09d7cc-bda4-4fe6-b650-75f008f13ada","16bcd965-011b-440d-a6db-a0573a57ec42","7ef45bee-dc2b-4a8c-9b9b-9ba437f4081e","e45eb5fa-af32-47e3-86dd-8f5e3a11dbbd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787186672978472001,"uuid":"1c48e389-82dc-4d29-ad73-ab18879f46a7"}